ent practices inhibit competition. The inquiry is preliminary, the FTC has no=
t announced an enforcement action, and Epic denies anticompetitive conduct. <=
a href=3D"https://www.statnews.com/2026/08/14/epic-systems-ftc-review-nda-use=
-possible-anticompetitive-practices/" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:=
underline;">STAT, =E2=80=9CEpic=E2=80=99s alleged anti-competitive practices =
under scrutiny,=E2=80=9D August 14, 2026</a> and <a href=3D"https://www.healt=
hcareitnews.com/news/epic-responds-potential-ftc-antitrust-probe" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Healthcare IT News, =E2=80=9CEpic res=
ponds to potential FTC antitrust probe,=E2=80=9D August 18, 2026</a>. (<a hre=
f=3D"https://www.statnews.com/2026/08/14/epic-systems-ftc-review-nda-use-poss=
ible-anticompetitive-practices/?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;t=
ext-decoration:underline;">statnews.com</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Why it matters</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Last week=E2=80=99s view=E2=80=94that =
Epic is turning interoperability into workflow infrastructure=E2=80=94was str=
engthened operationally but qualified competitively. Embedding payer rules at=
 order entry can reduce authorization-related cancellations, manual portal wo=
rk and avoidable denials. Yet the more workflows depend on Epic-mediated data=
 access, the more consequential its commercial and technical access policies =
become.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Strategist implication</strong=
></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Near term, Epic gains leverage over au=
thorization vendors because it controls clinician workflow and can offer heal=
th systems a lower-friction implementation path. Longer term, an access remed=
y or stronger interoperability enforcement could improve the position of neut=
ral third-party applications. Payers should therefore avoid Epic-only designs=
 and measure whether CRD deployment progresses to complete documentation, sub=
mission and appeal workflows.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Formal FTC action, if any; payer adopt=
ion beyond initial connections; and evidence that DTR and PAS reduce missing-=
document denials rather than simply accelerating requirement checks.</p>
