n pulls prior authorization into the revenue-cycle operating system</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">On August 18, R1 agreed to acquire Hum=
ata Health, an AI-enabled prior-authorization company, and integrate it into =
R1=E2=80=99s Phare operating system across authorization, utilization review,=
 documentation and coding. Transaction value was not disclosed. <a href=3D"ht=
tps://www.r1rcm.com/newsroom/r1-to-acquire-humata-health-enhancing-phare-os-w=
ith-ai-powered-prior-authorization-automation-and-payer-provider-collaboratio=
n" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">R1, =E2=80=9CR1 to Acqu=
ire Humata Health,=E2=80=9D August 18, 2026</a>. (<a href=3D"https://www.r1rc=
m.com/newsroom/r1-to-acquire-humata-health-enhancing-phare-os-with-ai-powered=
-prior-authorization-automation-and-payer-provider-collaboration?utm_source=
=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">r1rcm.com</a>)<=
/p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Why it matters</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Authorization is moving upstream from =
denial management into claim construction. R1 can now connect whether approva=
l was required, what evidence the payer requested, what was submitted, how th=
e service was documented and whether the eventual claim was paid correctly.</=
p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Strategist implication</strong=
></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">This confirms that pre-bill authorizat=
ion is becoming a core RCM platform module, not a standalone administrative t=
ool. Providers should expect bundled contracting around authorization-related=
 denials, cash acceleration and staff touches. Independent authorization vend=
ors will increasingly need payer connectivity, differentiated clinical-policy=
 intelligence or distribution through EHR and RCM partners.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The strongest product KPI is no longer=
 =E2=80=9Ctouchless authorization rate.=E2=80=9D It is the downstream combina=
tion of first-pass approval, avoided cancellations, clean claims, lower appea=
l volume and net collection yield.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Customer migration from existing R1 wo=
rkflows, payer participation and disclosed outcome metrics after integration.=
</p>
